tongue|mouth-part|NOUN|movable part inside the mouth|The soft movable part inside the mouth used in tasting, moving food, and forming speech.|lưỡi|She touched the loose tooth with her tongue.|Cô ấy dùng lưỡi chạm vào chiếc răng lung lay.|Countable; the tongue can name the organ generally, while my tongue names a person's own.|0
tongue|language|NOUN|language used by a community|A language, especially one associated with a person's home or community.|tiếng; ngôn ngữ|His grandmother tells stories in her native tongue.|Bà của anh ấy kể chuyện bằng tiếng mẹ đẻ.|Countable; native tongue and mother tongue are established expressions. This language use is more literary than language alone.|1
web|spider-threads|NOUN|network made by a spider|A structure of fine threads made by a spider, often used to catch insects.|mạng nhện|A web stretched between the two branches above the path.|Một mạng nhện giăng giữa hai cành cây phía trên lối đi.|Countable; a spider's web names the structure, not the spider itself.|0
web|online-system|NOUN|linked pages accessed through the internet|The system of connected pages and resources that people access through the internet.|mạng web|The museum put its opening hours on the web.|Bảo tàng đăng giờ mở cửa lên mạng web.|Usually the web in this sense; on the web describes online availability. Not every internet service is part of the web.|1
chew|break-food|VERB|break food with the teeth|To work food between your teeth so that it becomes easier to swallow.|nhai|He chewed the bread slowly while listening to the story.|Anh ấy nhai bánh mì chậm rãi trong lúc nghe câu chuyện.|Transitive chew food or intransitive chew slowly; chew on can also name what is being bitten.|-
habitual|regular-pattern|ADJECTIVE|done regularly as a habit|Done or experienced repeatedly as part of an established habit.|thường lệ; thành thói quen|Her habitual early arrival gave her time to unlock the hall.|Thói quen đến sớm thường lệ giúp cô ấy có thời gian mở khóa hội trường.|Usually before a noun such as behaviour or lateness; repetition does not itself imply addiction.|-
motorcycle|motor-powered-bike|NOUN|two-wheeled motor vehicle|A road vehicle with two wheels that is powered by a motor.|xe máy; mô tô|They parked the motorcycle beside the repair shop.|Họ đỗ xe máy cạnh tiệm sửa chữa.|Countable; ride a motorcycle describes operating or travelling on it, rather than drive a motorcycle in ordinary usage.|0
